  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/cyphocharax-multilineatus-4/",
      "html": "<p>This species belongs to the Curimata-relationship. At first glance it strongly resembles the well-known headstander (Chilodus punctatus), but it can easily be recognised by the black stripe through the eye. Moreover, Cyphocharax swims in a \"normal\" horizontal way.</p><p>Maximum length reported for the species is about 10 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/cyphocharax-multilineatus-4/",
      "html": "<p>The fish were obtained from Venezuela.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/cyphocharax-multilineatus-4/",
      "html": "<p>Cyphocharax feed on Aufwuchs and spend the whole day searching stones, roots and plants for algae and the small animals inside them.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/cyphocharax-multilineatus-4/",
      "html": "<p>C. multilineatus are very peaceful towards each other.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/cyphocharax-multilineatus-4/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Cyphocharax: from ancient Greek, means \"Charax with a hump\"; Charax is another genus of tetra. multilineatus: Latin, means \"with many stripes\". Chilodus: ancient Greek, means \"with teeth on the lips\". punctatus: Latin, means \"spotted\".</p><p>Suggested common name: Golden Mascara Tetra.</p>"
    }
  ],
